{% extends '@layout/default.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Installing AlmaLinux 10 in WSL2: PHP, MariaDB, Composer, PhpMyadmin{% endblock %}

{% block page_title %}
    <div class="mb-2 text-uppercase small fw-bold text-primary tracking-wider">How to's</div>
    <h1 class="fw-bold text-dark display-6 mb-0">Installing AlmaLinux 10 in WSL2: PHP, MariaDB, Composer, PhpMyadmin</h1>
    <hr class="mt-4 mb-2 opacity-25">
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>With the recent release of <a href="https://almalinux.org/blog/2025-05-27-welcoming-almalinux-10/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">AlmaLinux OS 10</a>, we have created a new recipe for our WSL development environment. Compared to its predecessor, AlmaLinux 10 provides performance enhancements, security updates and improved hardware support.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What You Get</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Like for <a href="https://www.dotkernel.com/php-development/almalinux-9-in-wsl2-install-php-apache-mariadb-composer-phpmyadmin/" data-type="link" data-id="https://www.dotkernel.com/php-development/almalinux-9-in-wsl2-install-php-apache-mariadb-composer-phpmyadmin/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">AlmaLinux 9</a>, the WSL recipe sets up the development environment with all the components a regular PHP developer needs:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>WSL2 - Windows Subsystem for Linux.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>AlmaLinux 10 - Free and open source Linux distribution.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>PHP - General-purpose scripting language geared towards web development.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Apache - Free and open-source cross-platform web server software.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>MariaDB - Community-developed, commercially supported fork of the MySQL relational database management system.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Git - Distributed version control system.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Composer - Application-level dependency manager.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Node.js - JavaScript runtime environment.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>PhpMyAdmin - Open source administration tool for MySQL and MariaDB.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Requirements</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Make sure that you have the <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/install#prerequisites" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">minimum requirements for running WSL2</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>OS-wise you must be running:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>Windows 10:<!-- wp:list -->
<ul class="wp-block-list"><!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>For x64 systems: Version 1903 or later with Build 18362.1049 or later.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>For ARM64 systems: Version 2004 or later with Build 19041 or later.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list --></li>
<!-- /wp:list-item -->

<!-- wp:list-item -->
<li>or Windows 11.</li>
<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>
<!-- /wp:list -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Hardware-wise, you need virtualization support. On some older hardware that supports this feature, it may be disabled from the BIOS.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>WSL2 needs Virtual Machine Platform feature enabled. You can enable it via the PowerShell running as an Administrator:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:enlighter/codeblock -->
<pre class="EnlighterJSRAW" data-enlighter-language="generic" data-enlighter-theme="" data-enlighter-highlight="" data-enlighter-linenumbers="" data-enlighter-lineoffset="" data-enlighter-title="" data-enlighter-group="">dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:VirtualMachinePlatform /all /norestart</pre>
<!-- /wp:enlighter/codeblock -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Installing the distro</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Start by downloading and installing the Linux distro with this command:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:enlighter/codeblock -->
<pre class="EnlighterJSRAW" data-enlighter-language="generic" data-enlighter-theme="" data-enlighter-highlight="" data-enlighter-linenumbers="" data-enlighter-lineoffset="" data-enlighter-title="" data-enlighter-group="">wsl --install -d AlmaLinux-10</pre>
<!-- /wp:enlighter/codeblock -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If everything ran ok, you are asked to enter a password at the end.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Next run each of the <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.org/development/v2/setup/setup-packages/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">ansible playbook commands</a> to install the development components.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading -->
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Using WSL2 with AlmaLinux 10</h2>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>You can start AlmaLinux10 by executing this coomand in the Windows Terminal:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:enlighter/codeblock -->
<pre class="EnlighterJSRAW" data-enlighter-language="generic" data-enlighter-theme="" data-enlighter-highlight="" data-enlighter-linenumbers="" data-enlighter-lineoffset="" data-enlighter-title="" data-enlighter-group="">wsl -d AlmaLinux-10</pre>
<!-- /wp:enlighter/codeblock -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Our PHP projects can be run by navigating into the root project folder and running this command:</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:enlighter/codeblock -->
<pre class="EnlighterJSRAW" data-enlighter-language="generic" data-enlighter-theme="" data-enlighter-highlight="" data-enlighter-linenumbers="" data-enlighter-lineoffset="" data-enlighter-title="" data-enlighter-group="">php -S 0.0.0.0:8080 -t public</pre>
<!-- /wp:enlighter/codeblock -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>Then you need to navigate to <code>http://localhost:8080</code> in your preferred browser.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:heading {"level":3} -->
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Running the Application Via Virtual Hosts</h3>
<!-- /wp:heading -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>An <strong>easier way</strong> to run your applications is via virtual hosts. The full instructions to set up your virtual hosts are in the <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.org/development/v2/virtualhosts/create-virtualhost/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Create virtualhosts page</a>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>After you set up your virtual hosts and install your project in e.g. the <code>/var/www/example.localhost/html</code> folder, you can run the application in the browser by accessing <code>example.localhost</code>.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

<!-- wp:paragraph -->
<p>If you run into any issues, make sure to first check our <a href="https://docs.dotkernel.org/development/v2/faq/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">FAQ page</a>. If all else fails, <a href="https://github.com/dotkernel/development/issues" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">create an issue</a> with details and we can talk.</p>
<!-- /wp:paragraph -->

